{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"smoking-bereft-boar","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff, which owns `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. These 14 entries move to `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/pid-liveness.args`, which this bug owns.\n\n`rebar._store.lock_owner._pid_alive` (`src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py:253-274`) returns True whenever signal 0 is not a liveness probe (`_signal_zero_probes_liveness`), which is the Windows case. So a dead holder reads as `pid_state=unverified-live`, stamps are never proven stale, and dead-owner reclamation falls back to the exclusive-leg proof or the age ceiling. Tests asserting a dead holder is detected fail (`pid_state=not-running` expected, `unverified-live` received), and `tests/interfaces/store/test_atomic_ticket_dir_create_021d.py::_dead_owner_stamp` loops `while lock_owner._pid_alive(pid)` until pytest's timeout kills the process (serial runs 44676069202 and 44678245519 died there and at `test_stale_lock_reclaim_write.py`).\n\nEvidence: Windows runs on throwaway branch `tmp/w05-remeasure` with origin/main `717c50f8b33` code plus a selection-only workflow change: run 44665461131 (the 242 `unclassified.args` entries; 48 passed, 194 failed or errored) and run 44681457334 (the 194, xdist, JUnit XML with full tracebacks). Both 2026-11-19 PST.\n\nModules:\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_atomic_ticket_dir_create_021d.py` (1)\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_stale_lock_reclaim_write.py` (1)\n- `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py` (6)\n- `tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_timeout_names_holder_7084.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_sync.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084.py` (1)\n\n## Approach\nDecide between a Windows liveness probe (`OpenProcess` + `GetExitCodeProcess`, which can prove a pid gone) and skipping these tests on Windows with the documented conservative behaviour. Either way the deselected lines leave `pid-liveness.args`.\n\n## Scope\nTest or product code for the listed modules, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/pid-liveness.args` (remove each fixed line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `pid-liveness.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `pid-liveness.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.\n","id":"c7b2-e4ed-37fd-4f60","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: tests that need a provably dead pid cannot pass, because _pid_alive answers alive on Windows"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795153682479061001,"uuid":"6e0e56a2-736f-498b-95d7-c6894582d8b9"}